#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:5
#: 03e2d33447c8433eb88d51f8fd2d73c5 23ce09874a50443885f83bc8b8aeb09e
#: 6c16b79d049a48718166ebf3c94e21b7 78a55a5a58cb45f7a3761ae934e65f5f
#: 97d9b497782a418cb6cb1feb0feca184 c559686fb0e5415aabe4161cdd213721
#: ced59cb08c2744798e4d8ea48b0e84ed
msgid "Diagnosing some common problems using Logs"
msgstr "使用日志诊断常见问题"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:7
#: 2ff9c0c933ba447d89eb953ab5a955ae 3785cab21766490ab6b3a8897cf49639
#: 5f114f9de7c943d08b48b02da1ef4668 c00a1c10aa5145fb83001dd9d931d824
#: c61e29820c7e4cca8878971224dde747 e2a6b6d8f94f46429b7a51323070ce15
#: eb6f25fdcb4040fdb4bd9b5dfaa8ccb5
msgid ""
"This page show how to diagnose the six most common problems affecting Copter"
" in particular but to some extent Plane and Rover as well."
msgstr "本页介绍如何诊断影响Copter（以及在一定程度上影响Plane和Rover）的六类最常见问题。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:14
#: 12cadeb40c4346268a27f0fc54d4fbbf 2a3227bd549c42618a4833f46fc65e38
#: 2c3488470b4541f9831072994caee6f1 3a297d6e4fce44fb9f95a16092fd288a
#: 78a99bc15ea34d4495b9db21725d2dbb a17918da6b9740e4a110e83f439905f1
#: e4355ba976064dcfa64114559df5f0d7
msgid "Mechanical Failures"
msgstr "机械故障"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:16
#: 12e5397ee3684787bbbe3123e60fa69c 185a7099627546cdbf4cd6ffd86f52a4
#: 37f745b8715b474d96a10a1ce1ce1cac 3f0fb194d21f4d5bb86cb7fb5193f8f9
#: 899ea41c961c458aa526666f957e349f f0da4a6f21d84a40b7d151a61e6b5cee
#: fcf2ef23e85043ae88507c01c2c1c77f
msgid ""
"Common mechanical failures include a motor or ESC failure (`including ESC "
"sync failures <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hBUBbeyLe0Q>`__), the "
"propeller breaking or coming off, etc.  These appear in the log as a sudden "
"divergence in the desired roll and pitch vs the vehicle's actual roll and "
"pitch.  This divergence is visible by graphing the ATT message's DesRoll vs "
"Roll, DesPitch vs Pitch and to a lesser extent DesYaw vs Yaw."
msgstr ""
"常见机械故障包括电机或ESC失效（`包括ESC同步失败 "
"<https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hBUBbeyLe0Q>`__）、螺旋桨断裂或脱落等。这些故障在日志中表现为期望横滚/俯仰与飞行器实际横滚/俯仰之间突然出现偏差。可通过绘制ATT消息中DesRoll与Roll、DesPitch与Pitch以及（次要地）DesYaw与Yaw的对比图来观察此偏差。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:21
#: 1050249257bb4f9a9d477e9eb691938a 1d44bf639fbe42909eeb64d417f548e7
#: 5bea60a59d534333acac7cc835644a64 71b7bb1466144a76befecdbe78d232ae
#: b7d308a5e82b4b158c44c461602e6db9 bc9a707a087d460d923b3ce4faec62f5
#: d58dd04f09bb4f02815bf9391e8a75f4
msgid ""
"In the example above the vehicle's actual roll (\"Roll\") closely follows "
"the desired roll (\"DesRoll\") for the first part of the log but then "
"suddenly diverges.  The autopilot wanted the roll to remain level (\"Roll\" "
"= 0) but it was unable to likely meaning there was a mechanical failure.  "
"This is very different from a software failure in which the autopilot "
"freaked out and for some strange reason suddenly wanted the copter up-side-"
"down because in such cases the DesRoll would be also be crazy and actual "
"Roll would follow."
msgstr ""
"在上例中，飞行器实际横滚值（「Roll」）在日志前段紧随期望横滚值（「DesRoll」），随后突然偏离。飞控希望横滚保持水平（「Roll」= "
"0），但无法做到，这很可能意味着发生了机械故障。这与软件故障截然不同——软件故障会导致飞控异常，莫名其妙地期望飞行器倒置，此时DesRoll也会同样异常，实际Roll也会跟随。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:23
#: 158d268e383947d598b33f75da8aa7b9 37ff9bc2887448059e7bf5d8632dffdc
#: 6e284e65f7364083a2e754995cc714b1 aac65e488f3145ec8680ba0a4d094aec
#: b296c17a6afe452fa7b30d3059dec343 cca16fc65d66467c9336d31e44819594
#: d3c5c18281f9419fafd8dbfa6c84785d
msgid ""
"Tlogs contain the same data.  Compare NAV_CONTROLLER_OUTPUT's nav_roll "
"(desired roll) and nav_pitch (desired pitch) to ATTITUDE.roll (actual roll) "
"and pitch (actual pitch)."
msgstr ""
"Tlog中包含相同数据。将NAV_CONTROLLER_OUTPUT的nav_roll（期望横滚）和nav_pitch（期望俯仰）与ATTITUDE.roll（实际横滚）和pitch（实际俯仰）进行比较。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:28
#: 147bbda8ceca4abf897d2ba2eb54b485 57264bbb022f4dc3876d69c2e395a62f
#: 8913e439575a4f37891965fedda0ff59 9b1677494c284b858bbaadab2e21bbda
#: c901b441aa2a4cc8b3669fd7cddee931 e0f16c9ae7a343e69aedd8bf05460c3e
#: fb14ba4364954dd398fe7938f4079df6
msgid "Vibrations"
msgstr "震动"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:30
#: 334575ccb9694948b03f1e33ebd66f7b 38fde2ea61464ad4a9812070757a3e85
#: 7f769837f38e436eaee597a5b0fc38f9 8b742310e482496faccdf768ddccd596
#: 9fff07096b82422586990fe0252045b7 ace3ed5593db4f00a9775130e3688fba
#: bc2a4f5cb1f74ca29828f4808acd3e90
msgid ""
"High vibrations can cause the Copter's accelerometer based altitude and "
"horizontal position estimates to drift far off from reality which leads to "
"problems with altitude hold (the vehicle may rocket into the sky) or "
"position control in modes like Loiter, PosHold, Auto, etc."
msgstr ""
"高震动会导致Copter基于加速度计的高度和水平位置估计严重偏离实际值，进而引发定高问题（飞行器可能急剧爬升）或Loiter、PosHold、Auto等模式下的位置控制问题。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:32
#: 0fd668b51fa74b41956c6c97c8d3c75c 16ffb6501d0c4cb6a867f151222386ca
#: 219ccb10f4bb4ecebb6ea9b124a3acc3 2dae46f496b7409ab4e211062777b590
#: 6eaed987a5c54eeea11b2acd4fe70358 8a6ad4a7172a43f496ebcc364e777761
#: c018aa37c03c4c2bbf4ee445217bb1bc
msgid ""
"As covered on the :ref:`Measuring Vibration <common-measuring-vibration>` "
"page, vibrations are best viewed by graphing the **VIBE** message's "
"**VibeX**, **VibeY** and **VibeZ** values.  Vibration levels below 30m/s/s "
"are normally acceptable. Levels above 30m/s/s may have problems and levels "
"above 60m/s/s nearly always have problems with position or altitude hold."
msgstr ""
"如 :ref:`测量震动 <common-measuring-vibration>` 页面所述，最好通过绘制 **VIBE** 消息的 "
"**VibeX**、**VibeY** 和 **VibeZ** "
"值来查看震动。震动水平低于30m/s/s通常可接受；高于30m/s/s可能出现问题；高于60m/s/s几乎总会出现位置或定高问题。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:34
#: 079c95cbb6e84aad9b6f3b012c971866 1945a22548f04e73852926115ab973ce
#: 468ccfecad914597a0f648be3dd9a2bd 4ab3e1a6bda4406594feb2d4485e2036
#: 8ca9fb80540c44c08ce0e966f7c9d07b 9e4663165a6e4bc48e25f648cac10116
#: d703c087bb7242889f427dacbc32cad7
msgid ""
"The below graph shows acceptable vibration levels which are consistently "
"below 30m/s/s"
msgstr "下图显示可接受的震动水平，始终低于30m/s/s"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:39
#: 01f655d6bf7b440fb046a991b87d4e81 3409b0cc112743b69e0f134302e545c9
#: 3d16a907cd40440bac9db8c1c802242a 5870bb68dce04e1eb3147cdde84774d1
#: af9a42e6e77d471ab0f8f4790be7b9c9 b6faa8c3cf224100b4bd540893ca250d
#: fff3891da04b4ddf842f770f39eefcd2
msgid ""
"The graph below is from a vehicle that had position estimation problems due "
"to high vibrations"
msgstr "下图来自一架因高震动而出现位置估计问题的飞行器"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:44
#: 1d62991f1dbf4ce4a89040b6b21e10b4 60d20dd9d0d04e7bac467fe9f62d25bd
#: 8cc9cef6bd2047b7a1afd597b87566f7 c16220776ec745b69dc6a87b78584757
#: ce15b3e0cdcb4ec7b9f5931c252fc322 df987291b7764e4a90913ed98836f440
#: e60927dd5ef94ab888c28fca74f60346
msgid ""
"Tlog's VIBRATION **vibration_x**, **vibration_y** and **vibration_z** can "
"also be used and show the same information as is stored to the dataflash log"
msgstr ""
"Tlog中的VIBRATION **vibration_x**、**vibration_y** 和 **vibration_z** "
"也可使用，其显示信息与存储在dataflash日志中的相同"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:52
#: 18477ed11ca045cf838f3f61ca2261c3 56e8daefb649421a90933646a0f9e680
#: 7a2c4f4e39244d42965a45cbaedb5287 9623d71c1c764551bf70d3870ec759b0
#: 99f57b2bb97742779e9adf9d142c9762 ab20252da81947d2a559883bf58c53c3
#: ab2c959879f740e891dad41da78bc181
msgid "Compass interference"
msgstr "罗盘干扰"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:54
#: 05c46344f4264f12a69934b2a1b307ec 3ca3bee8d29044b89ddd162c0bf5267a
#: 4fca565a668c49e3a65799c125e52b37 673f094734a84d189d49287765fd3909
#: aa5da3e6d48947c68cf5ef073fcd975e ac720fa867e0415ea50ddc0637c28f54
#: c1f4f15554d74f259f61b23cd4609b4b
msgid ""
"Interference from the power distribution board, motors, battery, ESCs and "
"other electrical devices near the autopilot can throw off the compass "
"heading which can lead to circling (aka \"toilet bowling\") or even the "
"copter flying off in completely the wrong direction.  Graphing the tlog's "
"mag_field (found under \"CUSTOM\") and throttle (found under VFR_HUD) is the"
" easiest way to quickly see the amount of interference."
msgstr ""
"电源分配板、电机、电池、ESC及飞控附近其他电气设备产生的干扰会使罗盘航向偏差，导致飞行器绕圈（俗称「冲马桶」）甚至朝完全错误的方向飞行。绘制tlog中的mag_field（位于「CUSTOM」下）和油门（位于VFR_HUD下）是快速查看干扰量的最简便方法。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:56
#: 0782ee6cb3b14e40b9d200ddd7551edf 3b496bd4d2844727a27529b691a4aefa
#: 7c9c65bb43254bf4929b20a7d20311c4 81504134d8e6479aac0974502765a2cb
#: bd5e5aa9c6d7493890850d97a46155ac cb619878c2344d6799c557bb105b636b
#: cefc98209f954bb084a9ddded3ab4cdd
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
"The graph below shows an acceptable amount of magnetic interference with "
"mag_field fluctuations of only 10% to 20% when the throttle is raised.  "
"Below 30% interference is acceptable.  Between 30% ~ 60% is in the grey zone"
" where it might be OK (some users are OK, some are not) and really bad "
"magnetic interference will show up as jumps of over 60% when the throttle is"
" raised."
msgstr ""
"下图显示可接受的磁场干扰量——油门拉升时mag_field波动仅为10%至20%。低于30%的干扰可接受；30%至60%处于灰色地带（有些用户没问题，有些有问题）；非常严重的磁场干扰会在油门拉升时出现超过60%的跳变。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:61
#: 0053c24701584cdcb176616df50ced2c 2a160d5ee56c4ab6aa851246bd463a77
#: 4460906554a249a5b4a5dd49f310e4a7 7be7d474945449cfa1593815076bf5d9
#: a0062e3b22464461827843836985e6d9 e31ef7f9cd96499791763f1079809f81
#: fa9cc7a4df9f45e9bb205eff82033069
msgid "Extra Notes:"
msgstr "额外说明："

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:63
#: 19dbafd6f5ad4e93a618ca90f87364e9 491a21b5dd7f4f2f8507ee3ae5daea3c
#: 513b3af44c0047389293b25cf74e2bba 5153fcd08d5445919c74e42e85977779
#: 60bbfa36a7184e1497d5391c9bc7812d 87034d4dbc484168b1125a13d724b9df
#: f15dfd18b2ce42cd8e8fe9582349d4dd
msgid ""
"The length of the mag_field can be anywhere from 120 ~ 550 depending upon "
"where in the world the vehicle is but it is normally around 330"
msgstr "mag_field的幅值因地理位置不同而在120至550之间变化，通常约为330"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:64
#: 33862c84ff3f40809cef31adcbb19979 34b3276888ab4fe7a65e425077aca030
#: 43855866ecdf48e4bf881a4539e6eabc 4df2bcd0f0124c3baaa7679af412aecb
#: bb702cc881dc4b519d9e7da4b1a63d45 bd4dc909010445b892f546247baa0dd4
#: c2c27fb123974e35b771492e0d9811d0
msgid ""
"The magnetic interference as a percentage of the total mag field is also "
"displayed at the end of the compassmot set-up procedure.  Search for "
"\"CompassMot\" on the :ref:`Advanced Compass Setup page <common-compass-"
"setup-advanced>` page to learn more about compassmot"
msgstr ""
"干扰磁场占总磁场的百分比也会在compassmot校准过程结束时显示。请在 :ref:`高级罗盘设置页面 <common-compass-setup-"
"advanced>` 中搜索「CompassMot」以了解更多关于compassmot的信息"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:65
#: 0f857051abb54376a742203733a2c5a7 1a35dc08064946448bca97355930a9db
#: 2f5ec133c8d4418f8e151add068a5c71 49459d8480864cf4b37e48d0b6c74075
#: 970f997f4e6d4431b71007623dbd4ea2 9a49132d9cd745c6a239b06b1b0618ec
#: cebf020bdc0645da8d54ccaae3fa0a7e
msgid ""
"Dataflash log's COMPASS message hold the compass's raw x, y and z axis "
"values (called MagX, MagY, MagZ) which are equivalent to the tlog's RAW_IMU "
"xmag, ymag and zmag fields.  It is possible to calculate the mag-field "
"length by first loading the dataflash log file into excel, filtering by the "
"COMPASS message and then calculating the mag-field using the formula "
"mag_field = sqrt(MagX^2, MagY^2, MagZ^2).  Note that the COMPASS message is "
"not enabled by default in the dataflash logs because it runs at 50hz and "
"does affect CPU performance a bit."
msgstr ""
"Dataflash日志的COMPASS消息包含罗盘原始x、y、z轴值（称为MagX、MagY、MagZ），与tlog中RAW_IMU的xmag、ymag和zmag字段等价。可通过将dataflash日志文件加载到Excel中，按COMPASS消息筛选，然后使用公式mag_field"
" = sqrt(MagX^2, MagY^2, "
"MagZ^2)计算磁场幅值。注意，COMPASS消息默认未在dataflash日志中启用，因为它以50Hz运行，会对CPU性能产生一定影响。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:66
#: 02a8f51a2cf24ebd916a69fab9a0b37a 19d5897bd474446dbdff8e42bddcdfe7
#: 4d8a042aef7a46cda066a0578a383367 747b3be0d7af4fbdb1c9a9591b71b4e2
#: b9b1bc1d8724425daa56b1ba046120da ddb701fdd50d4665bee2f69d36ffa55b
#: ec986bb5400c408b834bea566f6acbe6
msgid ""
"The image above it shows a short spike at the beginning of the graph but "
"this can be ignored because it is before the throttle is raised so it is "
"probably just as the user plugged in some other electrical device"
msgstr "上图在图表起始处显示一个短暂尖峰，但可忽略，因为此时油门尚未拉升，很可能只是用户插入了某个其他电气设备所致"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:71
#: 0f6dfac1fa804fd6bd2a1e448b9e3f10 2afef04a2243422a951cb16ca43dde30
#: 6330511439a64c648bb744125129350e 827c3db3412644c6869a820e34d461bb
#: 8c263d9a522a4047a5e1015a7ddd8a33 8ecdc69c52554dbdb4723d023ed53f7a
#: 97121924b94b4d47b86a6ea7623a55e0
msgid "GPS glitches"
msgstr "GPS信号异常"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:73
#: 1820673dd00b4557a97461337fc67ce8 6e5bad809d344a23950517b202684f6a
#: 859f31451c3d458386f3702ad780977e 93fa6b18d6e648e991612995899aa34c
#: 9723c6e22a5d4667b9a8c84104ecf1ee a07c0fe716924967afe8e705b01ea3c9
#: a323821c677a4752aff04768be06d7e7
#, no-python-format
msgid ""
"When in autonomous modes (Loiter, RTL, Auto, etc) position errors from the "
"GPS can cause the vehicle to think that it is suddenly in the wrong place "
"and lead to aggressive flying to correct the perceived error.  These "
"\"glitches\" show up in both the tlogs and dataflash logs as a decrease in "
"the number of satellites visible and an increase in the `hdop "
"<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dilution_of_precision_%28GPS%29>`__."
msgstr ""
"在自主模式（Loiter、RTL、Auto等）下，GPS位置误差会导致飞行器误认为自己突然偏离了正确位置，并进行激进飞行来纠正感知误差。这些「异常」在tlog和dataflash日志中均表现为可见卫星数减少以及"
" `hdop <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dilution_of_precision_%28GPS%29>`__ "
"增大。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:75
#: 0648076c0fa049ebacedc3c0537968de 2cac218689104538a626dd0ac0ef5d80
#: 553b1c2283504384b299cd3fc84f0a92 abe1bb77a9504176979b82a94cd345bf
#: cb97ccf9379a4c5996f020507926cd47 dc4279d644d14162813fcecc8560d00d
#: ef76d02ce9aa4c17aaf5e5e8e77e0148
msgid ""
"Graph the Dataflash log's GPS message's \"HDop\" and \"NSats\" values.  Hdop"
" values below 1.5 are very good, values over 2.0 could indicate the GPS "
"positions are not good.  The number of satellites falling below 12 is also "
"bad.  A significant change in these two values often accompanies a GPS "
"position change."
msgstr ""
"绘制Dataflash日志GPS消息中的「HDop」和「NSats」值。HDop低于1.5表示非常好，高于2.0可能表示GPS位置不可靠。卫星数低于12也是不良信号。这两个值的显著变化通常伴随着GPS位置跳变。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:80
#: 50d6c025bfce4d2a94d38dccdfe1ba51 5673e258f0d5448f9caba384863aed29
#: 6138f029553b4a2d846d3101bdb00dd1 8c691f669f7f4aa583a8a12fdcec9703
#: 94d20c1ad519498696d240af1042cffb c652143c21404023ac3284b3050bc096
#: dfc50774e179496da1df4921c818411e
msgid ""
"If using tlogs graph the GPS_RAW_IT group's \"eph\" and "
"\"satellites_visible\" values.  Hdop values below 150 are good, values over "
"200 could indicate a bad position."
msgstr ""
"若使用tlog，绘制GPS_RAW_IT组的「eph」和「satellites_visible」值。HDop低于150表示良好，高于200可能表示位置不可靠。"

#: ../../source/docs/common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs.rst:85
#: 089de2a5c0a0415283a729b8d15104dc 0eca3b9065b34ffd8a584476be298bc4
